Enumeration AssessmentReportingMethod
    documentation 'The method that the instructor of the class uses to report the performance and 
                  'achievement of all students. It may be a qualitative method such as 
                  'individualized teacher comments or a quantitative method such as a letter or a 
                  'numerical grade. In some cases, more than one type of reporting method may be 
                  'used.
    item Achievement/proficiency level
    item ACT score
    item Adaptive scale score
    item Age score
    item C-scaled scores
    item College Board examination scores
    item Composite Score
    item Composite Rating
    item Composition Score
    item Grade equivalent or grade-level indicator
    item Graduation score
    item Growth/value-added/indexing
    item International Baccalaureate score
    item Letter grade/mark
    item Mastery level
    item Normal curve equivalent
    item Normalized standard score
    item Number score
    item Pass-fail
    item Percentile
    item Percentile rank
    item Proficiency level
    item Promotion score
    item Ranking
    item Ratio IQ's
    item Raw score
    item RIT scale score
    item Scale score
    item Standard age score
    item Standard error measurement
    item Stanine score
    item Sten score
    item Theta
    item T-score
    item Vertical score
    item Workplace readiness score
    item Z-score
    item Other
    item Not applicable
    item Quantile Measure
    item Lexile Measure
    item Vertical Scale Score
